# Build context exclusions for the backend/ context.
#
# Both images are built with `context: backend`, so this is the file Docker
# actually reads:
#   * the API image      -> compose `context: backend`, dockerfile: Dockerfile
#   * the scientific one -> bimos setup, context = backend/dockers/..
#
# Two goals: keep the context small, and make sure no local artefact is ever
# what a build consumes. A stale .venv or node_modules inside the context is
# the classic way to ship an image that only works on the maintainer's machine.
#
# NOTE: the API builder stage does `COPY pyproject.toml README.md ./` and
# `COPY bimos ./bimos`, so those three paths must never be listed here.

# --- Python -----------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
.venv/
venv/
.mypy_cache/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov/
.tox/

# --- Node / frontend --------------------------------------------------------
node_modules/
dist/
.vite/

# --- local build trees ------------------------------------------------------
# GROMACS and Vina are compiled inside the image, and the wheel is built by the
# builder stage; a local tree must never be picked up instead.
build/
mutants/

# --- tests and developer tooling --------------------------------------------
# The images install the bimos package itself, never the test suite.
tests/
.coveragerc
.pre-commit-config.yaml

# --- secrets -----------------------------------------------------------------
# H-03: `.env` holds the real database URL and tool paths. No stage in this
# repository does a broad `COPY . .`, so the file cannot reach an image today,
# but nothing stops the next Dockerfile from adding one. Excluding it here makes
# the guarantee structural instead of incidental.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
secrets/

# --- caches and editor noise ------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
*.swp
.idea/
.vscode/
